<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>Select a widget in the dashboard designer to change its settings on the right.</FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="For everyone">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Greeting</strong>: says hello to whoever is signed in.</li>
            <li><strong>Digital Clock</strong>: 24-hour, date and milliseconds options.</li>
            <li><strong>Text Area</strong>: your own formatted text.</li>
            <li><strong>Announcements</strong>: live announcements for the viewer's location, pinned first.</li>
            <li><strong>My Training</strong>: the viewer's own courses.</li>
            <li><strong>My Shifts</strong>: the viewer's upcoming shifts, and optionally time off.</li>
            <li><strong>Who's On Today</strong>: who's working at a location today, and optionally who's clocked in.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="For managers">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Time Off to Approve</strong>: requests waiting for the viewer.</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance at a Glance</strong>: overdue training and expired or expiring documents.</li>
            <li><strong>Demand and Staffing</strong>: labour hours per game, and the hours most out of line with staffing.
                If your company uses Parties, it also shows the parties, children and party games in the range, and
                hours with a party on are never listed as out of line.</li>
            <li><strong>What's On Today</strong>: today's parties, children and staff on, and the parties still to come. Click
                one to open it, or <strong>View the day</strong> to open <a href="/manage/whats-on">What's On</a>. Select it in the designer
                to set how many to list and, for Admins, which location.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Venue technology">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Laser Game Status</strong> and <strong>Laser Scoreboard</strong>: the current game for a client.</li>
            <li><strong>Hall of Fame</strong>: top scores, best accuracy and team totals for a period.</li>
            <li><strong>Music Playlist Selector</strong> and <strong>Music Timeline</strong>: choose a playlist, see what's
                playing, and skip.</li>
            <li><strong>Projection Status</strong>: what's showing on a screen, with optional pause, skip and stop. When
                you set it up (and a projection <strong>Button</strong>), the # button beside <strong>Screen</strong> shows
                each screen's number on the kiosk for 8 seconds, so you can pick the right one.</li>
            <li><strong>Button</strong>: runs a projection program action, such as start, pause or next step. Only
                Admins and Managers can press it.</li>
            <li><strong>Automation Rule Status</strong>: whether a rule is on and when it last ran. Admins can turn it on
                or off.</li>
            <li><strong>Kiosk Health</strong>: which kiosks are online, struggling or offline.</li>
            <li><strong>Operations Alerts</strong>: the open alerts for the locations you manage, with Acknowledge and
                Resolve. Select it in the designer to show only warnings and critical alerts, or hide ones someone has
                acknowledged. On a kiosk dashboard nobody is signed in, so it shows no alerts.</li>
            <li><strong>Checklists Today</strong>: today's checklists where the viewer is working, with how many tasks are done
                and whether each is overdue. Select it in the designer and choose <strong>Widget settings…</strong> to hide
                checklists that are already done. On a kiosk dashboard nobody is signed in, so it asks you to sign in.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
